=== Code investigation (read, no live-browser access) ===

Read services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts:
  terminateExistingSessionsForUser() (line ~1393) — confirmed this is the
  mechanism that produces reason:"superseded_by_new_session". It sends a
  `session_ended`/`new_session_started` message over BOTH the SSE
  (sseResponse.write) and WS (sendWsMessage) transports before closing the
  connection — i.e. it DOES notify the client, cleanly, before killing it.

Grepped for every "type: 'session_ended'" emitter across the gateway repo:
  - orb-live.ts:1413/1425 — terminateExistingSessionsForUser (confirmed above)
  - orb-live.ts:12770 — POST /stop (handleLiveSessionStop's sibling route)
  - live-session-controller.ts:2274 — handleLiveSessionStop
Read both POST /stop handlers' docstrings/context: both are explicitly
"explicit user-initiated stop (POST /session/stop)" responses — i.e. BOTH
are echoes of a stop the CLIENT itself already initiated. Cross-referenced
against orb-widget.js's _sessionStop(): it detaches SSE/WS handlers
(onopen/onmessage/onerror = null, then close()) BEFORE POSTing /session/stop
(comment explains this ordering exists specifically so a manual close
can't trip auto-reconnect via onerror) — meaning by the time either of
these two responses could arrive, the client isn't listening anymore.
CONCLUSION: terminateExistingSessionsForUser is the only live path that
sends 'session_ended' to a client whose handlers are still attached.

Grepped orb-widget.js for `case 'session_ended'`:
  -> single occurrence, inside _handleMessage(msg) (shared WS+SSE dispatch
     per VTID-03471), calling _sessionStop() unconditionally.

Read _sessionStop() (async function _sessionStop()) in full (~90 lines):
  - Line 2299: `_s._userInitiatedStop = true;` — set UNCONDITIONALLY at
    the very top, regardless of caller/reason.
  - Confirmed via grep that _userInitiatedStop gates ~12 separate reconnect
    checks throughout the file (all meant to mean "the user explicitly
    left, don't background-reconnect").
  - Confirmed _sessionStop() never touches _s.overlayVisible, _root.style,
    or calls _setStatus()/_updateUI() with a new caption — unlike _hide(),
    which does all of these synchronously.

Read the case block immediately above session_ended in the same
dispatcher (connection_issue/live_api_disconnected, line ~2793): its own
PRE-EXISTING comment reads "We never auto-_sessionStop here; killing the
orb forces a page refresh." — i.e. this exact anti-pattern was already
named and avoided one case block up; session_ended was the one case that
still did it.

Read _hide() in full again (function _hide()): confirmed it does NOT
check any "was this user-initiated" flag before running — sets
_userRequestedClose=true, stops audio synchronously, sets
overlayVisible=false + _root.style.display='none', calls _updateUI(),
persists continuity, then calls _sessionStop() (which is fine INSIDE
_hide() — _hide() deliberately intends a full close, not a silent
reconnect suppression bug).

=== Implementation ===
Edited services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:
  case 'session_ended': replaced `_sessionStop();` with `_hide();`,
  with an inline comment recording the full investigation trail (why this
  is the only reachable case, what the two compounding defects were, and
  why the adjacent case block's own comment already named this exact
  anti-pattern).

